We have the key to ssh into the next level, we just need to extract it to our local computer.
Lets get the path directory first.
    bandit13@bandit:~$ pwd
    /home/bandit13
    bandit13@bandit:~$ exit
    logout
    Connection to bandit.labs.overthewire.org closed.
    root@ubuntu:~$ 
we exit back to our ubuntu server

We can use the SCP command to transfer the key from the bandit server to our local one
    root@ubuntu:~$ scp -P 2220 bandit13@bandit.labs.overthewire.org:/home/bandit13/sshkey.private .
the . at the end refers to the current working directory, it can be replaced for any other destination.

    root@ubuntu:~$ scp -P 2220 bandit13@bandit.labs.overthewire.org:/home/bandit13/sshkey.private .
